From e3f3f36b168e0a46cf75ab3431db2fa6123e31f0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gemini Mainline Experiment <gemini-mainline@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 21 Jul 2026 21:27:29 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] soc: mediatek: enable MT6797 A72 power sequence

Replace the read-only MT6797 A72 observer with a built-in singleton
provider. It installs a sleepable CPUHP prepare callback before CPU
bringup. The callback verifies exact DT CPU membership, CPU1 and the
first-cluster offline state, fixed 1.0V Vproc, and a live snapshot of an
explicitly userspace-open and active MTK watchdog before hardware writes.

Reproduce the audited fixed-state sequence: preserve CA7 CPU1 reset
release, perform the ordering read, coordinate PWRAP reset and DA9214
BUCKB, clear external-buck isolation, and request the 1.1V SRAM setting
through the private firmware service. Then let generic PSCI issue
CPU_ON and program MP2 DCM immediately on success. Deliberately omit
DVFSP and iDVFS.

Failures before isolation balance only this attempt regulator reference
and deassert reset. Once isolation has been touched, firmware has been
called, or CPU affinity is uncertain, leave shared power on, fault the
provider, and reject retry. PSCI failures and CPUHP teardown use
AFFINITY_INFO when firmware provides it. CPU off remains unsupported.

Keep provider integration readiness distinct from the runtime watchdog
gate. active-v1 and hooks_armed describe statically installed
integration. CPUHP prepare and the final pre-PSCI check each take a live
watchdog ownership/status/register snapshot. The AF diagnostic retains
its sole watchdog fd without closing it across the CPU request, making
those snapshots stable under the experiment contract; the helper does
not pin arbitrary userspace ownership.
---
